#### 8. GET `/api/nav/{schemeCode}/rolling-returns?periodInYears={n}`
Rolling returns for a single fund. One data point per trading day that has enough lookback history.

| Param | Type | In | Default | Range |
|-------|------|----|---------|-------|
| schemeCode | int | path | — | — |
| periodInYears | int | query | 1 | 1–30 |

**200:**
```json
{
  "schemeCode": 140085,
  "schemeName": "Nippon India ETF Nifty Next 50 Junior BeES",
  "fundHouse": "Nippon India Mutual Fund",
  "periodInYears": 3,
  "dataPoints": 1024,
  "minReturn": -8.45,
  "maxReturn": 32.67,
  "averageReturn": 14.23,
  "medianReturn": 13.87,
  "data": [
    { "date": "01-04-2026", "returnPercentage": 18.45 },
    { "date": "31-03-2026", "returnPercentage": 17.92 }
  ]
}
```

**400:** `{ "message": "periodInYears must be between 1 and 30." }`
**404:** `{ "message": "Fund with scheme code 999999 not found." }`

> `data` can have thousands of entries. **Always render as a line chart, not a table.** Summary stats (min/max/avg/median) can be shown in a legend/card.

